# No Markdown in AI-Generated Post Output

All AI-generated content (posts, captions, calendars) must be plain text only. Never include markdown formatting in post output.

## Forbidden in post content:
- **bold** syntax (double asterisks)
- *italic* syntax (single asterisks or underscores)
- Heading syntax (hash symbols)
- Code syntax (backticks)
- Link syntax
- Blockquote syntax (greater than signs)
- Horizontal rules (triple dashes)

## Where this applies:
- LLM prompts in content_planner.py — always include "Do NOT use any markdown formatting (no **, ##, backticks, etc). Write in plain text only." in every prompt that generates user-facing content.
- brain.py — same rule for single post generation.
- website_scraper.py — same rule for inferred profile output.
- The clean_markdown() function in content_planner.py should strip any remaining markdown as a safety net.

## Why:
Post content is displayed directly in the UI and copied to clipboard for use on social media platforms. Markdown symbols like ** render as literal characters and look broken.
